      "releaseNotes": "With the iOS 27 update, tapping a chord pad could give you the little buzz and then nothing, no sound, no colour. That's fixed. Every press plays instantly and lights up as it does.\n\n• Voice Leading, chords now move to their nearest notes instead of jumping register, so progressions flow instead of stepping. Switch it on under CTRL.\n• Play with both hands, hold a chord with one finger and press the next with another. Sliding between pads is smoother, and letting go of one hand no longer cuts the other's chord.\n• A tap always sounds, however briefly you touch the pad.\n• A much bigger joypad on iPhone SE, with more room to aim and more expression.\n• The Controls sheet is reorganised so it reads at a glance: the four pad modes, then the two locks, then Slide Chords and Voice Leading.\n• Recording stops when you leave the instrument or the app, so a take can't roll on unnoticed. Playing a take back stops when you leave Recordings.\n• The recording border now draws evenly all the way round, including the corners on larger iPhones.",
